@startuml fig06_class_simulator
!include theme.iuml
title Figure 6 — Class View: Discrete-Event Simulator and Validation (F-21 – F-24)

skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 50
skinparam wrapWidth 400

package "Shared with the live system — imported, not reimplemented" {
  interface DispatchPolicy <<interface>> {
    +choose(request : Request, node_states : list[NodeState], now : float, rng : Random) : NodeId
  }
  interface Clock <<interface>> {
    +now() : float
  }
  class Trace <<from Figure 5>> {
    +requests : list[Request]
    +checksum : str
  }
  class StageRecord <<from Figure 5>> {
    +req_id : str
    +queue_wait : float
    +service_prefill : float
    +service_decode : float
    +end_to_end : float
  }
}

package "Discrete-event simulator" #FFFCF5 {
  class DiscreteEventSimulator {
    -clock : SimClock
    -events : EventHeap
    -policy : DispatchPolicy
    -nodes : list[SimNode]
    +run(trace : Trace) : list[StageRecord]
  }
  class SimClock {
    +now : float
    +advance_to(t : float) : void
  }
  class EventHeap {
    +push(at : float, kind : ArrivalOrCompletion, req_id : str) : void
    +pop() : Event
  }
  class SimNode {
    +node_id : NodeId
    +queue : deque[Request]
    +in_flight : list[Request]
    +batch_capacity : int
    +tok_s_nominal : float
  }
  abstract class ServiceTimeModel {
    +{abstract} sample(r : Request, n : SimNode, rng : Random) : float
  }
  class FittedServiceTimeModel {
    +source : "measured hardware, Week 2"
    +prompt_length_terms : float[<= 6]
    +concurrency_term : float
    +noise : StochasticComponent
  }
  class StochasticComponent {
    +sigma : float
    +tau : float
    +sample(now : float, rng : Random) : float
  }
  DiscreteEventSimulator *--> SimClock
  DiscreteEventSimulator *--> EventHeap
  DiscreteEventSimulator *--> "1..*" SimNode
  DiscreteEventSimulator o--> ServiceTimeModel
  ServiceTimeModel <|-- FittedServiceTimeModel
  FittedServiceTimeModel *--> StochasticComponent
}

package "Validation (F-23)" #FFFCF5 {
  class Validator {
    +tolerance_pct : float
    +compare(sim : MetricSet, hw : MetricSet) : ValidationReport
  }
  class ValidationReport {
    +operating_points : int
    +p50_error : float
    +p95_error : float
    +within_tolerance : bool
    +validated_range : str
  }
  class SweepRunner {
    +axes : {R, load, staleness, policy, N}
    +run() : list[StageRecord]
    +label : "simulated"
  }
  Validator ..> ValidationReport : produces
  SweepRunner ..> ValidationReport : gated by
}

SimClock ..|> Clock
DiscreteEventSimulator o--> DispatchPolicy
DiscreteEventSimulator ..> Trace : consumes the identical trace (F-17)
DiscreteEventSimulator ..> StageRecord : emits the identical record shape
SweepRunner o--> DiscreteEventSimulator
Validator ..> DiscreteEventSimulator

note top of DispatchPolicy
  The simulator holds a **DispatchPolicy object**, not a copy of one. Any
  divergence between simulated and live routing is therefore a difference
  in service time or in state — never a difference in policy (F-21).
end note

note left of FittedServiceTimeModel
  Every parameter comes from the Week-2 calibration campaign: throughput against
  prompt length and concurrency, plus a noise term fitted to the measured variance
  envelope and autocorrelation time tau (F-22).
end note

note right of SimNode
  `batch_capacity` models llama.cpp's **fixed slot count exactly**, for every
  node in the pool — a fixed number of parallel sequences each holding a fixed
  KV share. It is not vLLM's dynamic paged-KV admission, where any integer
  capacity is emergent. A uniform engine removes that asymmetry, so no
  approximation is absorbed into the F-23 tolerance.
end note

note bottom of SweepRunner
  Runs only the axes hardware cannot reach — R beyond the physical pool ratio,
  N > 5, controlled staleness — and only after validation passes. Every figure
  it produces is labelled simulated (F-24, threat R2).
end note
@enduml
